    "problem_statement": "### TypeError when calling API methods with payload decorators\n\nHello! 👋\n\nI've encountered an issue with the `payload` decorator in the `tweepy/api.py` file. After applying a recent change, several API methods are throwing a `TypeError`. It seems like the arguments are being swapped incorrectly within the decorator, which is causing the methods to fail.\n\n#### Steps to Reproduce:\n\n1. Use the `payload` decorator on any API method, for example:\n   ```python\n   @payload('status', payload_list='statuses')\n   def get_status(self, id):\n       # method implementation\n   ```\n\n2. Call the decorated method:\n   ```python\n   api.get_status('12345')\n   ```\n\n3. Observe the `TypeError` being raised.\n\n#### Expected Behavior:\n\nThe method should execute without errors, correctly utilizing the `payload_list` and `payload_type` as intended.\n\n#### Actual Behavior:\n\nA `TypeError` is raised, indicating that the method arguments are not being handled as expected.\n\nThis issue seems to have been introduced in a recent commit where the `payload_list` and `payload_type` were swapped in the decorator. This affects multiple API methods, leading to failures across various functionalities.\n\nThanks for looking into this! 😊"
